{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Write this as a memorial in the book.</b> This section was spoken in the fortieth year, and the proof is that he said \"in the book,\" with the known meaning of the bet [prefix] — and it is the book of the Torah or another book that they had, called the Book of the Wars of YHWH, and it is not with us, just as we do not have the Book of Jashar, and the Midrash of Edu, and the Chronicles of the Kings of Israel, and the books of Solomon:" "And the meaning of \"in the ears of Joshua\" is that HaShem knew that he was destined to fight against the kings of Canaan:" "And the meaning of כי מחה אמחה — because he angered HaShem. For the chieftains of Edom were terrified by fear of Him because of the signs that He performed in Egypt and at the sea, and likewise Moab and Philistia. Now this Amalek heard of the might of HaShem on behalf of His people Israel, and came from a distant place to fight against Israel, and did not fear HaShem. And thus it is written: ולא ירא אלהים (Deuteronomy 25:18). And some say that Amalek was the name of the king, because Scripture says את עמלק ואת עמו (Exodus 17:13) — or another nation joined with him:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {0 "Resolved המדרש עדו as 'the Midrash of Edu,' an otherwise unknown work title; reading follows the text as given."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:35:24.883216972Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}